<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 33 0 R
/T (nanoCalc-GPT is a small transformer trained only on arithmetic examples, predicting the next token. I started with addition of two numbers and then extended the same model to all four operations \(+, -, *, /\). The central design goal was to stop the model from memorizing and force it to find the pattern. Every decision below comes from a problem I hit while training, and each one is a change to the data or the loss rather than to the model size.)
/E (nanoCalc-GPT is a small transformer trained only on arithmetic examples, predicting the next token. I started with addition of two numbers and then extended the same model to all four operations \(+, -, *, /\). The central design goal was to stop the model from memorizing and force it to find the pattern. Every decision below comes from a problem I hit while training, and each one is a change to the data or the loss rather than to the model size.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
